# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in only what you need. Nothing here is needed for the
# default flow: `make e2e-env-up && make e2e` runs against the local compose stack and the fake
# Google, with no secrets. Variables already set in the shell win.

# Mattermost under test. Defaults to the compose stack on localhost:8075 (SiteURL must be a
# redirect URI the OAuth client allows).
# PW_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8075
# The suite logs in as this system admin (created automatically on an empty server).
# PW_ADMIN_USERNAME=sysadmin
# PW_ADMIN_PASSWORD=Sys@dmin-sample1

# Compose stack ports and image (docker-compose.yml). The image is amd64-only; on Apple silicon
# Docker Desktop runs it under Rosetta.
# MM_IMAGE=mattermost/mattermost-enterprise-edition:12.0
# E2E_DB_PORT=5434
# E2E_FAKE_PORT=8090
# E2E_FAKE_HTTPS_PORT=8453
# E2E_DATABASE_URL=postgres://mmuser:mostest@127.0.0.1:5434/mattermost_test
# FAKE_GOOGLE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090

# Which Google the run talks to: fake (default; fake-google/ in the compose stack, no accounts or
# secrets) or real (the accounts below; start the stack with `make e2e-env-up E2E_GOOGLE=real`).
# `npm run test:real` sets real. The real lane is not exercised yet.
# E2E_GOOGLE=fake

# Real Google only. OAuth client the plugin is configured with; register
# http://localhost:8075/plugins/com.mattermost.gcal/oauth2/complete and
# http://localhost:8765/callback as redirect URIs.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# refresh_token (local Gmail, from `npm run google:auth -- owner|collab`) or dwd (Workspace, not implemented).
# GOOGLE_AUTH_MODE=refresh_token
# GOOGLE_OWNER_EMAIL=
# GOOGLE_OWNER_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# GOOGLE_COLLAB_EMAIL=
# GOOGLE_COLLAB_REFRESH_TOKEN=
